course: dictionary
lesson: 1714
title: One word, many meanings: circle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Circle can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). Context tells you which. «Draw a circle» names a shape, so it is a noun. «Circle the answer» tells you to do something, so it is a verb.
explain: «The plane circled the airport.» The plane is moving, and the airport is in the middle, so circled means flew round and round it. Always ask: what is the word doing in this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Teeth are brushed gently in small circles with a soft brush.» Small and gently tell you the circles are little round movements, not drawn shapes. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the author means.
fact: A circle is a round flat shape. Every point on its edge is the same distance from the middle, called the centre.
fact: The radius is the distance from the centre to the edge. The diameter goes edge to edge through the centre, and it is twice the radius.
fact: The circumference is the distance all the way around a circle.
fact: A circle of people or things is a group arranged in a ring, and a circle of friends is a group of friends.
fact: «Bon Odori» is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival, which honours the spirits of ancestors.
exercise: «Teeth are brushed gently in small circles with a soft brush.» What does circles mean here? | Long straight lines | Tight knots | *Small round movements | Loud noises
exercise: A circle is a round flat shape. Every point on its edge is the same distance from what? | The corner | The top | *The middle, called the centre | The sides
exercise: «The plane circled the airport.» What does circled mean? | Hid from it | Landed on it | *Flew round and round it | Crashed into it
test: «Circle the word that is NOT a noun.» What does circle mean in this question? | A dance in Japan | *To draw a ring around | A round flat shape | A group of people in a ring
test: «Bon Odori is a calm circle dance.» What kind of circle is this? | A line of straight tracks | Movement round and round a building | Round flat shape on paper | *A group of dancers arranged in a ring
exam: «She has a lovely circle of friends.» What does circle mean here? | A round shape drawn on paper | *A group of friends | To draw a ring around | To move round and round
